From e7173eb88ff0af0ac917c1673d53ad496207cfc6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=E5=AD=99=E5=A4=87?= <sunbei@sunbeideMac-mini.local>
Date: Tue, 26 May 2026 15:52:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] fix: normalize accepts[] amount fields
 (maxAmountRequired, amount, price)

This addresses TateLyman's review feedback about incompatible amount parsing:

- Normalize amount field using fallback chain: maxAmountRequired ?? amount ?? price
- Handle field semantics correctly:
  - maxAmountRequired: decimal style ("0.001"), convert by decimals
  - amount: atomic style ("1000"), keep as-is
  - price: legacy decimal style, convert for backward compatibility
- Add comprehensive tests covering both decimal and atomic shapes
- Improve error messages for missing/invalid amount fields

The live x402 services use different field names for the same concept:
- Decimal style: { "maxAmountRequired": "0.001" }
- Atomic style: { "amount": "1000" }
- Legacy style: { "price": "0.001" }

All three formats are now properly supported and converted to atomic units.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
